, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>::shrug:: <br /> <br /> Up to you if you want to duplicate work that other people (mostly Narm00) have long since been putting in on the book list.<br /> <br /> The Codex explicitly does <i>not</i> replicate material word-for-word from the source other than the names of traits for purposes of identification. That is <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Help:Purpose_and_Organizational_Direction\" target=\"_blank\">intentional</a>, as it is meant merely as an expanded cross-index to correctly identify the the location of the relevant passages at a glance across an entire library of books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T12:28:14-07:00","id":1095590,"title":"","content":"If it were just and index for cross reference, my reaction would be &quot;hey, that's awesome!&quot; If CofD had an OGL like Pathfinder, I'd be first in line to support it. That's not the case though, and yet I can see all of the mechanics for things like Attainments. It doesn't matter if you've reworded it or removed all the flavour text. It's an illegal reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Cha